A||||9||fiero56||poly mount thoughts?||||5||
Z||000000||fiero56||09-27-2000||11:46 PM||||Something that has always annoyed me with my Fiero 5-speed v-6, is how much the engine is able to rock under acceleration/deceleration. I have always wanted to install poly bushings, but haven't felt it worth the time and money until soon. I will be starting my "performance" 3.2L rebuild soon, and want to be able to finally eliminate this driveline "slack."<P>What does everyone think about all poly engine/tranny mounts on the Fiero. Poly dogbone, poly engine mount, poly tranny mounts? Too stiff? Too much engine vibration into the cabin? Too loud, and too many rattles? Break stuff prematurely? Great idea? Any other suggestions?||||reg||5
Z||000001||fiero56||09-28-2000||12:07 AM||||agh, too big.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pffsig1.jpg"> <p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 09-28-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||87ECO5||09-28-2000||07:39 AM||||You know my thoughts on it, pal - and I only have the poly bone!<P>Of course, I'm running a rougher engine than you are (and will be).||||reg||13
Z||000003||1FST2M6||09-28-2000||06:26 PM||||i'm very happy with the aluminum cradle mounts.. and poly dog bone.. the poly tranny and engine mounts are nice but not a real need for that much rigidity. the poly rear trailing arm bushings make a nice upgrade too.. my 86 SE would shake the mirror a bit but nothing i couldn't deal with.. and the current car (87 GT) doens't shake anything... i like them! ||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||09-28-2000||07:16 PM||||I'd do polly or solid cradle bushings and see what that does. Polly made a huge diferance in my car and it's just the 87 4 cyl. Even new rubber bushings will allow significant play in the cradle. not a good thing. Old ones can let it dance all over the place. Mine were in reasonably good shape but still to soft to be really stable.<P>Just replacing the old stock motor/tranny mounts with new ones will also stiffen it up allot. The rubber ones do get crappy over time no matter how good they may look.<P>Keep in mind..... Everyone says they got these huge improvments with polly A arm and motor mounts. What they don't take into account allot of time is that they are not compairing to new rubber ones. they are compairing to old crappy rubber ones that needed to be replaced anyway. When you compair polly to new rubber the diferance isn't always that great and the maintenance polly needs can be a real pain. <P>mantenance depends where the poly is. bushing with large movments, like suspension A arms and sway bars, need regular greasing or they can squeek like _____. Cradle and engine mounts don't rotate so they can't squeek. (They give you grease with the cradle set but you don't need it. If it's moving enough to squeek then something is way wrong.)<P>One place polly is proven to help nearly all cars is the sway bar. Mounting an anitsway bar in polly is like adding a heavier bar when compaired to performance of rubber bushings reguardless of new or old rubber. And poly sway bar bushings are cheap. Since sway bar bushings are generally out int the open maintenenace on them isn't much trouble.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 09-28-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||TheFiero64||09-28-2000||07:41 PM||||I have the poly "ultimate dogbone" & I love it.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Pontiaddict||09-28-2000||09:27 PM||||I just got a complete set of poly suspension bushings. I just installed the dogbone and it works great!<P>I'm gonna do the rest of the suspension over the weekend. (I hope)<P>Wish me luck and I'll tell you how it works when I'm done.||||reg||1
Z||000007||fiero56||09-28-2000||10:17 PM||||My Fiero is an '88, doesn't use/have cradle bushings, it's a solid mount to the frame.<P>I replaced all the engine/tranny mounts just a couple months ago, and even installed new poly-dogbone(FieroStore), and that setup did take out quite a bit of play, but there is still much more than I like.<P>What I want is if I hit the gas, I want the car to spring forward, not violently rock back and forth as the engine/tranny sloshes about. Same if I lift off the throttle, I wan't the car to suck down and slow, not kick forward and back as the engine/tranny moves about. <P>Maybe I'm just too picky, but I hate it when that happens.||||reg||1
Z||000008||BENGAL4||09-28-2000||11:32 PM||||Drew,<P>I would like to see you step on the gas hard just once. JK<P>Bill||||reg||10
